<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 1st century BCE</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the years 99–1 BCE: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 50 BCE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10256 5398" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 50 BCE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="7769" cy="1191" r="174"/><text x="7769" y="1264" font-size="209">1</text></g><g><circle cx="5304" cy="942" r="174"/><text x="5304" y="1015" font-size="209">2</text></g><g><circle cx="6141" cy="1232" r="174"/><text x="6141" y="1305" font-size="209">3</text></g><g><circle cx="5862" cy="1746" r="174"/><text x="5862" y="1820" font-size="209">4</text></g><g><circle cx="7165" cy="1820" r="174"/><text x="7165" y="1893" font-size="209">5</text></g><g><circle cx="5343" cy="1461" r="174"/><text x="5343" y="1534" font-size="209">6</text></g><g><circle cx="2331" cy="1704" r="174"/><text x="2331" y="1777" font-size="209">7</text></g><g><circle cx="5866" cy="834" r="174"/><text x="5866" y="907" font-size="209">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 50 BCE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Garamantian Empire &middot; Roman Republic &middot; Teotihuacan &middot; Bosporan Kingdom &middot; Kushite Empire &middot; Parthian Empire &middot; Han Dynasty &middot; Satavahana dynasty</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Thapsus</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Alesia</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Asiatic Vespers</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Social War (91–87 BCE)</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Third Mithridatic War</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Cantabrian Wars</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Julius Caesar</li><li>Strabo</li><li>Mithridates VI of Pontus</li><li>Pompey</li><li>Livy</li><li>Sulla</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>106–48 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>135–63 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>100–44 BCE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 64 BCE – c. 24 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 59 BCE – c. 17 CE</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 138–78 BCE</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the years 99–1 BCE, 61 recorded states were founded and 166 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Han Dynasty, the Roman Republic and the Parthian Empire. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 1st century BCE, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/1st-century-bce. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 1st century BCE</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Han Dynasty <span>206 BCE – 220 CE</span></li><li>Roman Republic <span>509 BCE – 27 BCE</span></li><li>Parthian Empire <span>247 BCE – 224 CE</span></li><li>Kushite Empire <span>1070 BCE – 350 CE</span></li><li>Satavahana dynasty <span>100 BCE – 220 CE</span></li><li>Garamantian Empire <span>1000 BCE – 700 CE</span></li><li>Teotihuacan <span>100 BCE – 550 CE</span></li><li>Bosporan Kingdom <span>438 BCE – 370 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Social War (91–87 BCE) <span>91–87 BCE</span></li><li>Asiatic Vespers <span>88 BCE</span></li><li>Third Mithridatic War <span>73–63 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of Alesia <span>52 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of Thapsus <span>46 BCE</span></li><li>Cantabrian Wars <span>29–19 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Julius Caesar <span>3: 100–44 BCE</span></li><li>Strabo <span>4: c. 64 BCE – c. 24 CE</span></li><li>Mithridates VI of Pontus <span>2: 135–63 BCE</span></li><li>Pompey <span>1: 106–48 BCE</span></li><li>Livy <span>5: c. 59 BCE – c. 17 CE</span></li><li>Sulla <span>6: c. 138–78 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
